WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.893
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:16.163 --> 00:19.416
[theme music playing]

3
00:26.590 --> 00:27.758
[liquid bubbling]

4
00:32.763 --> 00:35.474
[clinking, rattling]

5
00:35.558 --> 00:36.684
[cat meows]

6
00:37.643 --> 00:39.478
[hoofbeats]

7
00:41.397 --> 00:42.273
[water splashes]

8
00:49.154 --> 00:50.823
[handcuffs rattling, click]

9
00:55.202 --> 00:57.830
-[thunder rumbling] -[thunderclap]

10
00:57.913 --> 01:00.165
[low tense music playing]

11
01:00.249 --> 01:04.295
TAEKANG GROUP TASK FORCE MANAGING DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

12
01:07.047 --> 01:07.923
[strained grunt]

13
01:08.007 --> 01:10.968
[thunder rumbling]

14
01:15.848 --> 01:16.807
[strained breath]

15
01:19.977 --> 01:22.062
-[thunderclap] -[heavy breath]

16
01:26.984 --> 01:27.902
[man] Yoon Yi-jun?

17
01:29.778 --> 01:32.573
[panting]

18
01:32.656 --> 01:35.826
-[ominous music sting] -[heavy breathing]

19
01:40.497 --> 01:41.457
[grunts]

20
01:43.667 --> 01:44.877
[heavy exhale]

21
01:44.960 --> 01:48.255
[panting]

22
01:51.467 --> 01:52.718
[deep exhale]

23
01:59.642 --> 02:01.477
-[heavy breath] -[thunderclap]

24
02:08.984 --> 02:11.403
-[thunderclap] -[thunder rumbling]

25
02:18.494 --> 02:21.705
[low rumbling]

26
02:21.789 --> 02:23.999
FIVE HOURS AGO

27
02:24.083 --> 02:27.002
[pilot] Seoul Tower. Republic of Korea Air Force 01.

28
02:27.086 --> 02:29.922
Established on ILS Runway One-Niner.

29
02:30.005 --> 02:31.799
Requesting landing clearance.

30
02:37.972 --> 02:39.556
[traffic controller] The Republic of Korea Air Force One

31
02:39.640 --> 02:41.183
will be landing shortly.

32
02:41.976 --> 02:43.560
All ground vehicles and related personnel,

33
02:43.644 --> 02:45.854
please stand by at your designated positions.

34
02:46.647 --> 02:49.233
Runway One-Niner, clear to land.

35
02:49.316 --> 02:50.693
The Republic of Korea Air Force One…

36
02:50.776 --> 02:53.487
[reporter 1] The president and the economic delegation's Middle East tour

37
02:53.570 --> 02:55.823
is set to conclude today upon their return.

38
02:55.906 --> 02:58.575
In a rare move, the heads of the nation's top five conglomerates

39
02:58.659 --> 03:00.411
officially accompanied the president.

40
03:00.494 --> 03:02.162
-[reporter 2] Yoon Yi-jun, sir! -[reporter 3] Here they are.

41
03:02.246 --> 03:03.706
[reporter 1] Managing Director Yoon Yi-jun

42
03:03.789 --> 03:06.458
spearheaded the successful diplomatic efforts,

43
03:06.542 --> 03:09.670
which resulted in a surge in Taekang's share price.

44
03:10.254 --> 03:12.256
[reporter 4] Indeed, it was Mr. Yoon Yi-jun,

45
03:12.339 --> 03:14.466
the youngest member of the economic delegation,

46
03:14.550 --> 03:16.885
that caught the most attention, as he is slated

47
03:16.969 --> 03:19.388
to be the successor to Chairman Yoon Tae-sik,

48
03:19.471 --> 03:20.973
who has been in ill health.

49
03:21.056 --> 03:22.349
In this diplomatic mission,

50
03:22.433 --> 03:24.893
which aimed to highlight our economic partnerships,

51
03:24.977 --> 03:28.731
Mr. Yoon is credited with leveraging our nation's economic soft power

52
03:28.814 --> 03:31.316
-to elevate our standard. -[crowd applauding]

53
03:32.067 --> 03:34.737
Thank you for your hard work, Mr. President.

54
03:34.820 --> 03:36.864
Of course. Yes.

55
03:39.199 --> 03:40.034
Thank you.

56
03:42.536 --> 03:44.371
[camera shutter clicking]

57
03:44.455 --> 03:46.040
-[clicking rapidly] -[chimes]

58
03:51.170 --> 03:53.922
[dramatic percussive music playing]

59
03:56.216 --> 03:58.135
[hurried footsteps approaching]

60
03:59.011 --> 04:01.930
Here's your usual tea, steeped for 3 minutes at 90 degrees.

61
04:08.645 --> 04:09.980
[breathes nervously]

62
04:12.274 --> 04:13.609
88 degrees,

63
04:14.151 --> 04:15.861
-3 minutes and 10 seconds. -[beeps]

64
04:16.278 --> 04:17.529
[anxious exhale]

65
04:17.613 --> 04:18.655
I won't drink it.

66
04:19.406 --> 04:20.407
The photos.

67
04:22.743 --> 04:24.578
Your overseas trip was a success.

68
04:24.661 --> 04:25.704
Next.

69
04:25.788 --> 04:27.414
You helped the president uphold his authority.

70
04:27.498 --> 04:28.707
Stop.

71
04:28.791 --> 04:29.750
[Yi-jun] Zoom in.

72
04:31.001 --> 04:33.378
Your jawline's so sharp, you might cut someone with it, sir.

73
04:33.462 --> 04:35.130
You were the main character as usual.

74
04:35.214 --> 04:36.799
Is that the right answer?

75
04:37.424 --> 04:38.842
Uh, well…

76
04:42.012 --> 04:42.888
[gasps]

77
04:43.889 --> 04:46.183
This is great for the new Series 7 campaign.

78
04:46.642 --> 04:47.851
It's really a perfect shot.

79
04:47.935 --> 04:50.145
Leak this photo to every media outlet.

80
04:50.604 --> 04:51.688
Right.

81
04:51.772 --> 04:53.607
I see you have a plan for everything, sir.

82
04:53.690 --> 04:56.151
[assistant] I'll wrap it up in half an hour and get back to you.

83
04:56.235 --> 04:59.071
Oh, Attorney Kim Si-hyun said he'll be coming to pick you up, sir.

84
05:01.073 --> 05:02.074
[tires screech]

85
05:02.157 --> 05:03.325
[car door opens]

86
05:04.827 --> 05:05.828
[car door closes]

87
05:10.874 --> 05:12.000
SEOUL AIR BASE

88
05:12.084 --> 05:13.377
[Si-hyun] Oh, good Lord, man.

89
05:13.460 --> 05:16.088
As if winning a 3-trillion-won contract wasn't enough,

90
05:16.171 --> 05:19.091
you used the president as a prop for some free advertising?

91
05:20.467 --> 05:23.637
They rolled out the red carpet for us, the cameras were rolling,

92
05:24.471 --> 05:25.806
our models were effective.

93
05:25.889 --> 05:28.058
-Wow. -Why not, huh?

94
05:29.518 --> 05:31.520
-Guess I should take notes, hmm? -[phone buzzes]

95
05:31.603 --> 05:35.440
Watching you squeeze every little bit out of the day is inspiring.

96
05:35.524 --> 05:36.984
What? Is there something wrong?

97
05:37.860 --> 05:38.861
[Yi-jun] No.

98
05:38.944 --> 05:41.572
I'm just going over the PR photos Mr. An sent along.

99
05:42.030 --> 05:42.906
It's Mr. Jung.

100
05:42.990 --> 05:44.199
[quirky music playing]

101
05:44.283 --> 05:47.119
Not Mr. An, not Mr. Kim, it's Mr. Jung.

102
05:47.202 --> 05:49.204
He worked with you for five years on the TF team,

103
05:49.288 --> 05:51.790
and his name is Mr. Jung Da-woon.

104
05:51.874 --> 05:54.126
[sighs] Thanks for that useful tidbit.

105
05:54.209 --> 05:55.377
[sighs]

106
05:57.045 --> 05:59.506
I'll deliver the contract myself. Take me to the office.

107
05:59.590 --> 06:02.384
Also, tell me why you bothered to pick me up. I'm dying to know.

108
06:02.467 --> 06:04.136
[Si-hyun] Aren't you tired, honey?

109
06:04.219 --> 06:06.638
The least I can do is give you a comfy ride.

110
06:08.724 --> 06:11.560
[upbeat background music playing]

111
06:20.444 --> 06:23.572
-[humming] -[upbeat music playing over headphones]

112
06:33.498 --> 06:35.584
[gentle music playing]

113
06:49.973 --> 06:51.225
Are you all right?

114
06:53.518 --> 06:54.561
Ah…

115
06:54.645 --> 06:56.146
[customer 1] Thanks a lot.

116
06:56.563 --> 06:57.981
Um…

117
06:58.065 --> 06:58.899
Wow, no way.

118
06:58.982 --> 07:01.360
Can I add you on social media, oppa?

119
07:02.027 --> 07:03.153
I don't use social media.

120
07:03.237 --> 07:04.446
[customer 1] Oh…

121
07:04.529 --> 07:05.364
A couple ring.

122
07:05.447 --> 07:06.865
[man] I'm a police officer.

123
07:06.949 --> 07:08.408
This money will be safe in my hands.

124
07:08.492 --> 07:10.035
[elder] You really are a policeman, right?

125
07:10.118 --> 07:11.411
[man] Yeah, that's what I said.

126
07:11.995 --> 07:13.330
-Here… -[customer 2] Police officer?

127
07:13.872 --> 07:15.290
More like a piece of trash.

128
07:15.374 --> 07:16.583
[man] Take a look at this.

129
07:17.584 --> 07:18.752
-As for this money… -Oh…

130
07:18.835 --> 07:20.045
-…once the investigation's over-- -[customer 2] Hey.

131
07:20.712 --> 07:22.005
"Inspector Park"?

132
07:22.089 --> 07:23.340
Crap!

133
07:23.423 --> 07:24.925
[groans] Let me go!

134
07:25.008 --> 07:25.842
I got you. [grunts]

135
07:25.926 --> 07:27.261
-Are you okay? -[gasps]

136
07:27.344 --> 07:28.470
[elder] Oh, my money.

137
07:28.553 --> 07:29.721
-My money. He's got my money! -[phone buzzing]

138
07:29.805 --> 07:31.431
-Oh, no, what am I gonna do? -Hey, man.

139
07:31.515 --> 07:32.724
-Uh… -I'm at the convenience store.

140
07:32.808 --> 07:33.934
You…

141
07:36.603 --> 07:37.854
[sighs] Again?

142
07:38.522 --> 07:39.439
[customer 2] Hey!

143
07:40.565 --> 07:41.608
Hey!

144
07:44.403 --> 07:45.862
[man yelps] Leave me alone!

145
07:45.946 --> 07:47.281
[customer 2] Stop right there!

146
07:47.364 --> 07:48.949
[groans] Sheesh…

147
07:50.117 --> 07:51.368
Hey, punk!

148
07:52.744 --> 07:55.038
[man] Sir! Oh, we're in big trouble.

149
07:55.539 --> 07:56.540
The cops are here.

150
07:56.623 --> 07:58.041
-Then why'd you lead them here, you prick? -[groans]

151
07:58.125 --> 08:00.502
-Let's bounce! -Hurry up, let's go!

152
08:01.003 --> 08:03.547
-[car doors open, close] -[panting]

153
08:04.214 --> 08:05.132
[engine starts]

154
08:05.215 --> 08:07.551
-[tires screeching] -[engine revving]

155
08:08.385 --> 08:10.554
[car horns honking]

156
08:10.637 --> 08:11.722
-[button clicks] -[door whirring]

157
08:11.805 --> 08:13.015
[scammer 1] Who's this guy?

158
08:14.474 --> 08:16.810
You had me freaking out. I thought it was the fuzz.

159
08:17.352 --> 08:19.271
You seriously let that kid rattle you?

160
08:21.189 --> 08:22.858
Hand over the old lady's money.

161
08:22.941 --> 08:24.192
You're looking at around a year

162
08:24.276 --> 08:26.653
or a fine of at least three times the criminal proceeds.

163
08:26.737 --> 08:29.197
That's the expected punishment for voice phishing.

164
08:29.614 --> 08:32.826
I'm worried about today's youth. You learn that online?

165
08:33.327 --> 08:34.911
Come on, open that back up.

166
08:35.620 --> 08:36.621
-[joints cracking] -[scammer 1] Hey, let's roll.

167
08:36.705 --> 08:38.623
-[scammer 2] Yes, sir. -Sheesh.

168
08:40.250 --> 08:42.836
-[groaning] -Sir, sir! Sir, are you okay?

169
08:42.919 --> 08:44.087
Are you all right?

170
08:44.171 --> 08:45.380
-Let go, damn it! -[groans]

171
08:45.464 --> 08:46.965
Hey, wanna die?

172
08:47.049 --> 08:48.300
Is that what this is?

173
08:49.092 --> 08:50.052
Why, you…

174
08:50.135 --> 08:52.471
[scammer 1 grunting]

175
08:54.014 --> 08:55.557
You guys threw the first punch.

176
08:55.640 --> 08:58.518
As of now, I'm acting in self-defense. Got that?

177
08:59.144 --> 09:00.228
[fierce grunt]

178
09:00.312 --> 09:01.646
7TH SPECIAL MISSION UNIT

179
09:02.314 --> 09:03.899
-[groans] -[man] You punk!

180
09:03.982 --> 09:05.359
Sir! Sir!

181
09:05.942 --> 09:08.028
What are you doing? Kick this guy's ass.

182
09:09.905 --> 09:11.740
[grunts] Hey, who's this prick?

183
09:12.574 --> 09:13.950
Kick his a-- [groans]

184
09:14.034 --> 09:15.327
[man] You're dead meat, you hear me?

185
09:15.869 --> 09:17.287
[shouts]

186
09:17.371 --> 09:20.290
[upbeat action music playing]

187
09:26.171 --> 09:27.130
[groans]

188
09:27.214 --> 09:29.132
-Come on. Bring it. -[man] No, don't bring it!

189
09:29.966 --> 09:31.385
[man groaning]

190
09:34.221 --> 09:35.055
[scammer 3] Come on!

191
09:40.977 --> 09:42.562
-[beeps] -[scammer 1] Get him!

192
09:42.646 --> 09:44.106
[automated voice] Beginning car wash.

193
09:44.189 --> 09:45.816
-No, wait! -[customer 2] Time for a wash!

194
09:45.899 --> 09:47.901
[scammers grunting]

195
09:53.490 --> 09:55.033
[scammer 1] You bastard! [grunts]

196
09:56.618 --> 09:57.744
Why, you…

197
09:58.453 --> 10:00.539
[scammer 1 grunting]

198
10:03.375 --> 10:05.919
[upbeat jaunty music playing]

199
10:06.002 --> 10:08.505
-[scammer 1 grunts] -[man] I can't see.

200
10:09.005 --> 10:12.175
-[customer 2] He's over here! -I'm gonna knock you out, punk! [grunts]

201
10:14.845 --> 10:15.804
What's going on?

202
10:16.430 --> 10:18.140
-You bastard! -[frantic shouts]

203
10:18.640 --> 10:20.642
-Stomp him! -[scammer 1] Yeah! Stomp him!

204
10:21.893 --> 10:23.353
[screams]

205
10:23.437 --> 10:25.188
You've got the wrong guy!

206
10:26.648 --> 10:27.482
[scammer 4] Huh?

207
10:27.983 --> 10:29.317
Hey, over there!

208
10:29.401 --> 10:30.444
Hey!

209
10:31.111 --> 10:32.446
That's the guy!

210
10:41.163 --> 10:42.330
[shouts]

211
10:42.414 --> 10:43.915
[grunting]

212
10:50.046 --> 10:50.922
[shouts]

213
10:53.550 --> 10:54.551
[screams]

214
10:55.469 --> 10:56.636
[coughing]

215
10:59.514 --> 11:01.516
[distant siren wailing]

216
11:01.600 --> 11:03.310
[man screams] Help!

217
11:03.393 --> 11:04.352
Okay.

218
11:11.067 --> 11:13.028
What's this, Summer Swag? Yeesh.

219
11:13.111 --> 11:14.988
Where the heck did Gutsy Kang run off to?

220
11:15.071 --> 11:16.907
[man panting]

221
11:16.990 --> 11:18.492
You're making a bad choice!

222
11:19.451 --> 11:21.119
Stop chasing me!

223
11:21.203 --> 11:22.746
[panting] Yeesh!

224
11:33.215 --> 11:35.592
[Si-hyun] So, Legal got instructions from the chairman.

225
11:35.967 --> 11:38.512
He wants to finalize the succession process.

226
11:38.595 --> 11:41.556
You're gonna lead a new era for Taekang. How does that feel?

227
11:43.266 --> 11:44.643
[phone buzzing]

228
11:49.731 --> 11:50.565
[sighs]

229
11:50.649 --> 11:52.734
SECRETARY HAN

230
11:53.985 --> 11:55.654
[buzzing continues]

231
11:55.737 --> 11:56.738
[Yi-jun sighs]

232
11:57.572 --> 11:59.366
The chairman said something else.

233
12:00.408 --> 12:03.161
He wants you to stay out of trouble so everything goes smoothly.

234
12:05.330 --> 12:06.998
Isn't it about time you cleaned house?

235
12:07.082 --> 12:09.209
[tuts] Yeah, you're right.

236
12:10.043 --> 12:12.045
It's time I cleaned things up, I guess.

237
12:16.883 --> 12:18.802
-[tires screeching] -[groaning]

238
12:18.885 --> 12:20.679
-[tires screeching] -[Yi-jun grunts]

239
12:22.264 --> 12:23.974
-[groans] -[pedestrian 1] Oh, no!

240
12:24.057 --> 12:25.642
-Damn it! -[customer 2] You punk!

241
12:25.725 --> 12:26.601
[panting]

242
12:26.685 --> 12:27.519
[scared gasp]

243
12:28.770 --> 12:30.230
[tires screeching]

244
12:30.730 --> 12:32.482
[suspenseful dramatic music playing]

245
12:33.817 --> 12:35.026
[grunts]

246
12:38.530 --> 12:39.447
Whoa…

247
12:40.240 --> 12:42.117
[pedestrian 2] Are you hurt? Are you okay, sir?

248
12:42.200 --> 12:43.868
[man] No, I'm not okay. Move it!

249
12:45.370 --> 12:46.371
-Move! -[pedestrian 3] Hey!

250
12:46.454 --> 12:47.998
-[grunts] -[groans]

251
12:48.081 --> 12:50.917
[upbeat action music playing]

252
12:51.001 --> 12:52.502
[customer 2] I told you I'd get you, didn't I?

253
12:52.586 --> 12:54.004
Sorry. You all right?

254
12:54.087 --> 12:55.589
-[customer 2] Yeah. -That was crazy.

255
12:56.339 --> 12:58.216
[Si-hyun] Man, I nearly had a heart attack.

256
12:58.300 --> 12:59.593
That hyung is kind of cool though.

257
12:59.676 --> 13:00.635
Someone you know?

258
13:00.719 --> 13:02.804
Anyone who can fight better than me is a hyung.

259
13:03.597 --> 13:06.099
There's Dong-seok Hyung, Chan-sung Hyung, and now that hyung.

260
13:06.641 --> 13:07.976
-Besides, man, he-- -Let's get going.

261
13:08.059 --> 13:09.060
Huh? Right.

262
13:10.020 --> 13:11.563
[customer 2] Stop it.

263
13:11.646 --> 13:12.814
Hold still.

264
13:14.190 --> 13:17.027
-[panting] -[siren wailing]

265
13:27.454 --> 13:28.580
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

266
13:28.663 --> 13:30.081
EPISODE 1

267
13:30.165 --> 13:31.958
[humming]

268
13:32.876 --> 13:33.793
[sighs]

269
13:36.087 --> 13:38.840
MEN'S SHOWER

270
13:38.923 --> 13:41.509
-[clock ticking] -[detective whistling]

271
13:42.093 --> 13:44.304
[exclaiming] Whoa, holy crap! Damn it!

272
13:44.387 --> 13:45.513
You scared the hell out of me.

273
13:45.597 --> 13:46.473
Dude, you scared me.

274
13:46.556 --> 13:48.975
I told you to go to the jjimjilbang out front.

275
13:49.059 --> 13:49.976
Come on!

276
13:50.060 --> 13:52.312
They stop me every time I try to use the women's changing room.

277
13:52.395 --> 13:53.772
And they threaten to call the police too.

278
13:53.855 --> 13:55.231
I get where they're coming from.

279
13:55.315 --> 13:57.859
I also want to call the cops so they'll take you away.

280
13:57.942 --> 13:59.694
Ugh, why do you have to be so uptight?

281
13:59.778 --> 14:01.112
Would it kill you to wait just a minute?

282
14:01.196 --> 14:02.572
That's all I need for a shower.

283
14:02.656 --> 14:04.949
Anyways, when will they replace the tile in the women's shower?

284
14:05.033 --> 14:06.868
Why won't anyone listen to my complaints?

285
14:06.951 --> 14:09.454
I don't know, I don't know, okay? I'm not in charge of the complaints.

286
14:09.537 --> 14:11.414
Didn't you say you were done being single?

287
14:11.498 --> 14:12.999
How's that going for you?

288
14:13.500 --> 14:15.210
Well, I'm actually quite popular.

289
14:15.293 --> 14:17.587
[laughing]

290
14:17.671 --> 14:19.923
[comical music playing]

291
14:20.006 --> 14:22.217
You mean between the women who think you're a guy,

292
14:22.300 --> 14:24.636
or… did you mean the men who think you're a guy?

293
14:24.719 --> 14:26.638
I don't know what would cause that kind of confusion.

294
14:26.721 --> 14:28.890
You're the only one who finds it confusing!

295
14:28.973 --> 14:30.266
That's disgusting.

296
14:30.350 --> 14:31.393
Wait here.

297
14:31.476 --> 14:33.728
Oh, hey, Seok-jin! Come here! Chop-chop.

298
14:33.812 --> 14:34.854
Hurry up, man.

299
14:37.482 --> 14:38.608
That's right. Uh…

300
14:40.276 --> 14:41.194
You're our mascot.

301
14:41.277 --> 14:43.780
You're the investigative brains behind our unit.

302
14:43.863 --> 14:46.157
So give me an honest answer, man to man.

303
14:47.450 --> 14:48.993
When you first looked at her,

304
14:49.077 --> 14:50.704
you noticed her physique and thought,

305
14:50.787 --> 14:52.205
"Damn, he's manly!"

306
14:52.288 --> 14:53.206
Isn't that right?

307
14:53.289 --> 14:54.374
[sighs]

308
14:54.457 --> 14:56.710
Then working with her made you realize that she's practically a guy.

309
14:56.793 --> 14:58.128
-You know what I'm saying? -Stop it now.

310
14:58.211 --> 14:59.421
Never thought about it.

311
15:00.296 --> 15:02.799
[detective] Huh? You never thought about it?

312
15:02.882 --> 15:05.510
Hey, when will you start using that head of yours?

313
15:06.428 --> 15:08.012
-Treat that wound. -Oh, okay.

314
15:08.596 --> 15:09.597
[Seok-jin] Take care.

315
15:21.860 --> 15:23.528
-Want me to deliver it? -I got it.

316
15:23.611 --> 15:24.946
I'll head home afterwards.

317
15:25.029 --> 15:26.072
Um, Mr. Yoon…

318
15:26.156 --> 15:27.115
Next time.

319
15:29.743 --> 15:31.745
[soft ominous music playing]

320
15:31.828 --> 15:32.829
[Da-woon] Good luck, sir.

321
15:35.039 --> 15:36.583
-Anything else to report? -[door closes]

322
15:36.666 --> 15:38.376
No, not exactly.

323
15:38.460 --> 15:41.337
Then pack up and go. Clocking out on time is a priority.

324
15:43.673 --> 15:44.799
Go on without me.

325
15:48.553 --> 15:50.513
-[door closes] -[tuts]

326
15:50.597 --> 15:53.433
[rain pattering]

327
15:53.516 --> 15:56.436
[dramatic swelling music playing]

328
15:56.519 --> 15:59.481
CHAIRMAN YOON TAE-SIK

329
16:01.733 --> 16:03.359
[Yi-jun] I thought I said we should end things.

330
16:03.777 --> 16:05.695
[employee] I don't want things to end like this.

331
16:05.779 --> 16:07.155
Please, Mr. Yoon.

332
16:08.823 --> 16:09.908
[Yi-jun] Somehow…

333
16:10.700 --> 16:12.786
-you've got it all twisted. -[thunderclap]

334
16:13.369 --> 16:14.621
The only one who gets a say

335
16:14.704 --> 16:16.998
in how things start and end is me, Ms. Han.

336
16:17.081 --> 16:18.124
Mr. Yoon.

337
16:18.208 --> 16:19.375
Let's make this clean.

338
16:20.001 --> 16:20.919
How much do you want?

339
16:21.002 --> 16:21.920
[soft scoff]

340
16:23.671 --> 16:25.757
Do you really think I'm going to make this easy for you?

341
16:25.840 --> 16:28.468
I thought I told you to stop being so clingy.

342
16:29.385 --> 16:31.513
Next time, you won't get off with just a warning.

343
16:32.180 --> 16:34.182
[suspenseful music playing]

344
16:34.265 --> 16:35.600
What are you gonna do?

345
16:39.395 --> 16:40.480
I don't know yet.

346
16:40.939 --> 16:42.357
If you were to keep this up…

347
16:42.857 --> 16:45.276
well, there's just no telling what I would do to you.

348
16:45.860 --> 16:48.488
[dramatic music playing]

349
16:50.114 --> 16:52.534
-[thunderclap] -[thunder rumbling]

350
16:56.996 --> 16:59.165
-[sighs] -[phone buzzes]

351
17:06.756 --> 17:07.966
MISSED CALL SECRETARY HAN

352
17:08.049 --> 17:09.050
I'LL WAIT FOR YOU…

353
17:10.093 --> 17:12.011
[Ms. Han] I'll be waiting until you arrive.

354
17:12.095 --> 17:13.805
If you avoid me again,

355
17:13.888 --> 17:16.724
I'll report this to the chairman through his secretary.

356
17:18.643 --> 17:20.228
[deep, slow exhale]

357
17:26.025 --> 17:28.444
[Si-hyun] You're gonna lead a new era for Taekang.

358
17:30.280 --> 17:31.948
The chairman said something else.

359
17:33.408 --> 17:36.411
He wants you to stay out of trouble so everything goes smoothly.

360
17:39.747 --> 17:41.583
Isn't it about time you cleaned house?

361
17:41.666 --> 17:44.419
TAEKANG GROUP TASK FORCE MANAGING DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

362
17:57.390 --> 17:58.516
[Si-hyun] Yoon Yi-jun.

363
17:59.851 --> 18:02.729
[panting]

364
18:08.860 --> 18:10.570
-[heavy breath] -[thunderclap]

365
18:10.653 --> 18:12.822
[dramatic music continues]

366
18:29.589 --> 18:30.673
[camera shutter clicks]

367
18:31.841 --> 18:33.760
[camera shutter clicking]

368
18:35.053 --> 18:36.679
FORENSICS

369
18:36.763 --> 18:38.890
[Seok-jin] The victim's name is Han Eun-young.

370
18:38.973 --> 18:41.225
She was a secretary for the Taekang Group.

371
18:41.851 --> 18:42.977
She was strangled to death.

372
18:43.061 --> 18:44.812
The murder weapon was found on the scene.

373
18:45.438 --> 18:49.192
[Seok-jin] A black cowhide belt, 100 cm long and 3 cm wide.

374
18:50.068 --> 18:53.446
Yoon Yi-jun's prints were found on both the body and on the belt.

375
18:54.948 --> 18:58.826
Notably, no DNA evidence such as skin tissue or blood stains

376
18:58.910 --> 19:01.079
belonging to the perpetrator was found on the victim.

377
19:01.162 --> 19:03.623
However, judging by the defensive wounds found

378
19:03.706 --> 19:05.667
on the victim's fingernails and right leg,

379
19:05.750 --> 19:06.960
there's a pretty high chance

380
19:07.043 --> 19:09.295
the perpetrator is either left-handed or ambidextrous.

381
19:09.796 --> 19:10.964
And our prime suspect

382
19:11.047 --> 19:12.715
is TF Team's managing director,

383
19:13.549 --> 19:14.592
Yoon Yi-jun.

384
19:14.676 --> 19:15.718
SUSPECT

385
19:15.802 --> 19:17.679
YOON YI-JUN, 32-YEAR-OLD, MALE

386
19:18.513 --> 19:19.472
[grunts]

387
19:22.433 --> 19:23.434
Yeah.

388
19:24.644 --> 19:26.229
Except we don't have…

389
19:27.146 --> 19:28.189
a motive just yet.

390
19:28.272 --> 19:30.775
So currently, he's claiming innocence.

391
19:30.858 --> 19:34.445
Since it's a case involving a chaebol, it was handed to our agency.

392
19:35.905 --> 19:38.992
The thing is, his behavior is kind of an open secret.

393
19:39.659 --> 19:42.036
Everyone knows Yoon Yi-jun's a psycho.

394
19:42.120 --> 19:44.372
[frustrated scream] Again!

395
19:44.455 --> 19:45.581
Go prepare it again.

396
19:45.665 --> 19:46.833
[yells] Again!

397
19:46.916 --> 19:48.960
[detective] He's notorious for looking down on folks,

398
19:49.585 --> 19:52.797
and he throws a fit like a madman when things don't go his way.

399
19:53.923 --> 19:56.175
They say someone collapsed in front of him…

400
19:56.968 --> 19:58.678
[detective mimics Yi-jun laughing]

401
19:59.012 --> 19:59.929
…and he laughed.

402
20:02.932 --> 20:04.892
I bet you they were seeing each other.

403
20:05.560 --> 20:06.769
Makes sense, right?

404
20:08.438 --> 20:09.939
He probably had his fun,

405
20:10.440 --> 20:13.151
then broke things off with her when he got bored.

406
20:13.234 --> 20:14.819
[sighs]

407
20:15.403 --> 20:18.531
Man, I bet Ms. Han was totally heartbroken too.

408
20:18.614 --> 20:20.908
She just wanted to get back together.

409
20:20.992 --> 20:23.411
Hey, Wan-gu, would it kill you to stop writing novels

410
20:23.494 --> 20:25.163
and just stick to the facts for once?

411
20:25.246 --> 20:27.623
[captain] Are you seriously gonna spread rumors during our briefing?

412
20:27.707 --> 20:28.791
-[Wan-gu] Well… -[captain scoffs]

413
20:28.875 --> 20:29.792
…you know what they say,

414
20:29.876 --> 20:31.377
if a chimney's got smoke coming out,

415
20:31.461 --> 20:32.837
something started a fire!

416
20:32.920 --> 20:33.755
That's what.

417
20:33.838 --> 20:37.383
By the way, why are we bringing him in as a witness when he's a suspect?

418
20:37.467 --> 20:39.302
That's because the dude's lawyered up,

419
20:39.385 --> 20:41.971
so he's got a whole legal team saying he's clear.

420
20:42.472 --> 20:44.265
I told you to stop spreading rumors.

421
20:44.348 --> 20:46.017
You're just gonna get Jae-hee pissed off.

422
20:46.100 --> 20:47.727
Hold on a minute. What'd you say?

423
20:47.810 --> 20:49.145
[inhales sharply, clears throat]

424
20:49.896 --> 20:52.523
So he denies everything, even though his fingerprints were found

425
20:52.607 --> 20:54.108
at the crime scene and on the murder weapon?

426
20:54.192 --> 20:55.234
Yeah, exactly!

427
20:55.318 --> 20:56.319
Whoa…

428
20:57.445 --> 20:59.280
He's coming tomorrow, is that right?

429
20:59.363 --> 21:00.823
Yeah, that's right.

430
21:01.532 --> 21:04.202
Good. Just leave him to me, okay?

431
21:04.994 --> 21:07.580
Yoon Yi-jun, eh? You loser.

432
21:08.623 --> 21:11.709
I swear on my fist of truth, I'll bring you in.

433
21:11.793 --> 21:12.710
-[grunts] -[growling effect]

434
21:12.794 --> 21:14.087
7TH SPECIAL MISSION UNIT

435
21:25.598 --> 21:30.103
[distant siren wailing]

436
21:31.229 --> 21:32.563
[detective] This way, sir.

437
21:41.155 --> 21:42.698
At the scene, we found fingerprints

438
21:42.782 --> 21:45.243
on both the black belt and the victim's shirt,

439
21:45.326 --> 21:47.995
and Mr. Yoon, they were your fingerprints.

440
21:48.079 --> 21:48.996
I'm sure you know,

441
21:49.080 --> 21:51.666
but that's just circumstantial evidence, Detective.

442
21:52.250 --> 21:56.504
[Si-hyun] Having discovered Ms. Han first, he merely made contact to check on her.

443
21:56.587 --> 21:58.422
It's circumstantial, I know.

444
21:58.506 --> 22:01.175
But direct and indirect evidence hold the exact same weight in court.

445
22:01.259 --> 22:03.511
You should know that, so stop butting in.

446
22:03.594 --> 22:05.263
Regardless, plenty of people walk free

447
22:05.346 --> 22:07.598
because the prosecution doesn't have direct evidence.

448
22:07.682 --> 22:09.058
And I'm sure you're aware of that too.

449
22:11.853 --> 22:12.895
[captain sighs]

450
22:12.979 --> 22:16.190
Hey, why don't you answer me yourself? What's with the silent treatment?

451
22:40.089 --> 22:41.632
[papers rustling]

452
22:41.716 --> 22:43.634
"Judging by the direction of the defense wounds

453
22:43.718 --> 22:45.344
and the direction of the belt pressure marks,

454
22:45.428 --> 22:48.764
there's a high chance the perpetrator used their left hand to commit the crime."

455
22:48.848 --> 22:50.349
I see you're left-handed, right?

456
22:51.225 --> 22:53.436
Um, don't… don't you have anything to say?

457
22:59.066 --> 23:01.485
It seems all the evidence points in my direction.

458
23:02.028 --> 23:03.529
Even the fingerprints you found,

459
23:03.613 --> 23:06.073
they seem to be from someone who is left-handed.

460
23:07.867 --> 23:09.869
I guess we're in a little conundrum.

461
23:13.748 --> 23:15.124
So then, Detective…

462
23:17.376 --> 23:18.878
do you really think…

463
23:20.171 --> 23:21.214
I'm a killer?

464
23:21.756 --> 23:23.507
Do you really think that I killed her?

465
23:24.675 --> 23:27.386
[Wan-gu] You totally did, you damn murderer!

466
23:28.262 --> 23:30.348
Ugh, where the heck's Kang anyway?

467
23:30.890 --> 23:32.850
So much for her righteous fist of truth bullshit.

468
23:32.934 --> 23:33.976
She's on a business trip.

469
23:34.060 --> 23:35.019
Business what?

470
23:36.103 --> 23:38.105
She's giving a talk on fraud prevention.

471
23:38.189 --> 23:39.232
Ah.

472
23:40.816 --> 23:42.944
That was a good move on the captain's part.

473
23:43.486 --> 23:45.738
Her righteous fury might kill the suspect.

474
23:46.322 --> 23:48.908
[elder 1] My goodness, you have an appetite.

475
23:48.991 --> 23:51.244
Thank you for the meal. I should really get going now though.

476
23:51.327 --> 23:53.412
-Have some more pork. -[soft chuckle]

477
23:53.496 --> 23:54.413
More rice and vegetables?

478
23:54.497 --> 23:55.373
No, I'm good.

479
23:55.456 --> 23:57.458
-No, I'm really full right now. Thanks. -[elder 2] Hold on.

480
23:57.541 --> 23:59.252
-You can't possibly be full. -That's right.

481
23:59.335 --> 24:00.878
Here, have a little bit more meat.

482
24:01.879 --> 24:04.882
-Wow, it's so good. [clears throat] -Voice scamming sure is scary though.

483
24:06.259 --> 24:09.136
Okay, fine. Now, according to this,

484
24:09.220 --> 24:12.682
the cameras on the 32nd floor were under maintenance.

485
24:12.765 --> 24:13.933
Would you say that's correct?

486
24:14.016 --> 24:16.894
I understand they put out a notice regarding the maintenance schedule,

487
24:16.978 --> 24:20.064
so… I guess you knew the cameras weren't rolling that day, right?

488
24:20.147 --> 24:21.440
[Yi-jun] Mm-hmm.

489
24:21.524 --> 24:22.525
Actually…

490
24:23.567 --> 24:24.986
I had been away on business.

491
24:26.153 --> 24:27.154
Hmm.

492
24:30.324 --> 24:32.785
We have you clocking out at around 9:10 p.m.

493
24:32.868 --> 24:34.537
Why did you return to the office?

494
24:35.329 --> 24:37.248
She said she'd wait for me till I returned.

495
24:37.999 --> 24:39.875
If she couldn't go home 'cause of me…

496
24:41.085 --> 24:42.628
then I'd be a bad boss, right?

497
24:46.215 --> 24:47.049
Uh…

498
24:47.675 --> 24:49.260
were you in a relationship with her?

499
24:49.343 --> 24:51.053
Can you explain the rumors?

500
24:53.014 --> 24:53.889
No way.

501
24:54.932 --> 24:56.225
Did Ms. Han…

502
24:57.018 --> 24:59.145
have a crush on me?

503
24:59.228 --> 25:01.397
-[soft chuckle] -Mr. Yoon.

504
25:03.232 --> 25:06.193
If you keep this up, we won't be able to confirm your alibi.

505
25:06.277 --> 25:09.613
My client has the right to not be coerced into making any statements.

506
25:09.697 --> 25:12.366
And I've got the legal right to kick your legal ass out of this interview.

507
25:12.450 --> 25:15.703
Please refrain from asking my client so many loaded questions, Detective.

508
25:16.287 --> 25:18.706
Additionally, take note of his cooperation,

509
25:18.789 --> 25:21.334
despite your attempts to slander him with your questions.

510
25:21.417 --> 25:22.585
Besides, I think you know…

511
25:23.377 --> 25:25.421
you have no right to remove me.

512
25:25.504 --> 25:27.006
-[door opens] -Who the hell is…

513
25:33.679 --> 25:35.264
Are you nuts?

514
25:35.806 --> 25:37.224
Man, I'm stuffed.

515
25:37.308 --> 25:39.143
Wow. Just wow.

516
25:40.561 --> 25:41.896
-Loyalty. -[Jae-hee] Eh.

517
25:48.527 --> 25:50.780
Mr. Yoon, thank you for your cooperation.

518
25:51.822 --> 25:53.991
I sincerely want the case to be solved.

519
25:54.492 --> 25:55.659
So solve it.

520
25:56.243 --> 25:57.995
Of course. I'll walk you out.

521
26:01.707 --> 26:02.833
Solve it.

522
26:06.253 --> 26:07.922
I hate those guys.

523
26:14.011 --> 26:15.638
[dramatic music sting]

524
26:26.607 --> 26:29.777
[superior in angry voice] You summoned the heir to Taekang without telling me?

525
26:31.862 --> 26:32.863
We did, sir.

526
26:33.531 --> 26:34.949
Wouldn't you agree that Yoon Yi-jun

527
26:35.032 --> 26:36.784
is actually the prime suspect in this case?

528
26:38.911 --> 26:40.162
Captain Park.

529
26:40.246 --> 26:43.541
Why do you suppose I assigned this case to Special Investigations?

530
26:44.792 --> 26:46.961
I mean, your team is short-handed.

531
26:47.044 --> 26:49.255
You are all typically short on results.

532
26:49.338 --> 26:51.549
You are short on detective skills.

533
26:51.632 --> 26:53.050
You're even short on good looks!

534
26:54.051 --> 26:56.095
You guys always mess things up!

535
26:56.178 --> 26:59.557
This was my way of spoon-feeding your team a really easy win here!

536
26:59.640 --> 27:01.767
And make up for all the trouble you caused!

537
27:01.851 --> 27:02.852
[sighs]

538
27:06.272 --> 27:08.399
"Circumstantial suicide."

539
27:10.067 --> 27:11.277
Is that so hard?

540
27:13.112 --> 27:14.655
[soft sigh]

541
27:17.783 --> 27:20.035
Stop poking your nose where it doesn't belong.

542
27:21.579 --> 27:24.373
And you should learn which battles are worth fighting.

543
27:25.499 --> 27:26.459
[superior] Okay?

544
27:27.668 --> 27:28.544
[sighs]

545
27:28.627 --> 27:29.920
[sizzling]

546
27:30.004 --> 27:32.298
[Jae-hee] Wow. So, what's going on, sir?

547
27:32.756 --> 27:35.551
What, rich people can't be murderers? Huh?

548
27:35.634 --> 27:37.511
We're really gonna let this slide?

549
27:37.595 --> 27:40.222
Didn't you hear what they said earlier? We don't have any direct evidence.

550
27:40.306 --> 27:41.599
Oh, come on.

551
27:41.682 --> 27:43.267
[Captain Park] Man, whatever.

552
27:43.350 --> 27:44.935
Let's say we bring him in, what changes?

553
27:45.019 --> 27:47.480
Even the state can't touch Taekang, so what are we gonna do?

554
27:48.314 --> 27:49.815
Wow, shit!

555
27:49.899 --> 27:52.109
Doesn't the badge we wear deserve some dignity?

556
27:52.193 --> 27:55.446
We've got dignity, just no money. That's all.

557
27:55.529 --> 27:59.825
[loud groan] Someone please lend me 180,000 won!

558
27:59.909 --> 28:01.619
Sorry, folks. I'm sorry.

559
28:02.077 --> 28:02.995
[Wan-gu] Uh, Hyung, keep it down!

560
28:03.078 --> 28:05.247
Ah, those rich bastards can get away with anything.

561
28:06.248 --> 28:07.249
It's unfair, for real!

562
28:07.333 --> 28:08.667
-Sheesh. -[bottle thuds]

563
28:08.751 --> 28:10.794
-Let's have a drink. -You're not allowed. Put it down.

564
28:10.878 --> 28:12.546
-Huh? -Put the glass down.

565
28:12.630 --> 28:13.839
Really?

566
28:14.715 --> 28:15.633
[Captain Park] Huh?

567
28:20.012 --> 28:21.180
Come on. Just this once.

568
28:21.263 --> 28:22.097
[sighs]

569
28:22.181 --> 28:24.308
Sir… just this once.

570
28:24.391 --> 28:25.476
Just one sip.

571
28:25.976 --> 28:26.977
[groans]

572
28:27.061 --> 28:28.687
[Captain Park] Why the heck not?

573
28:28.771 --> 28:29.688
[Wan-gu] Let's go!

574
28:29.772 --> 28:31.023
[Captain Park] Whatever.

575
28:31.106 --> 28:33.484
-[Jae-hee gulping] -Hey, hey, hey, she's drinking all of it.

576
28:33.567 --> 28:36.362
-[Captain Park] She… Whoa, she… -[exhales]

577
28:39.281 --> 28:40.741
Sir, I'm here.

578
28:45.162 --> 28:48.374
[Wan-gu] Undercover work, you know, it's not easy.

579
28:48.457 --> 28:49.542
[deliveryman] I'm off, sir.

580
28:50.125 --> 28:51.752
[Wan-gu] Back in the day, I…

581
28:52.795 --> 28:54.421
Ugh, why do my lips keep going dry?

582
28:54.505 --> 28:56.507
-Son of a… -[Wan-gu] Hmm?

583
28:56.590 --> 28:58.759
[quirky music playing]

584
28:59.343 --> 29:01.512
-[Seok-jin] Kang Jae-hee! -[Wan-gu sighs]

585
29:02.846 --> 29:04.181
I knew this would happen.

586
29:05.391 --> 29:06.892
What are you doing? Go get her.

587
29:06.976 --> 29:09.019
Come on, Detective Kim went.

588
29:09.103 --> 29:09.937
[sighs]

589
29:10.020 --> 29:12.106
-[Captain Park] Punk! -[Wan-gu] Hey, Kang!

590
29:12.189 --> 29:13.857
Ah, come on, come back!

591
29:14.441 --> 29:15.442
[sighs]

592
29:19.446 --> 29:21.865
Why does he keep chasing people when he's had something to drink?

593
29:21.949 --> 29:24.201
Way back when, that kid, uh,

594
29:24.285 --> 29:28.247
lost something extremely precious due to a split-second hesitation.

595
29:28.872 --> 29:29.915
That's why…

596
29:30.833 --> 29:33.627
Jae-hee keeps kicking up a storm after having something to drink.

597
29:33.711 --> 29:36.046
Goodness, that's so sad.

598
29:36.130 --> 29:37.715
-[owner] Oh. -[gulps]

599
29:38.257 --> 29:40.009
Mm. What's our total?

600
29:40.092 --> 29:42.595
-184,000 won. -[sucks teeth]

601
29:42.678 --> 29:44.805
184,000.

602
29:44.888 --> 29:46.890
[Jae-hee] Ha! You thought you could get away from me?

603
29:46.974 --> 29:48.183
-What the hell are you doing? -[Jae-hee] Get off.

604
29:48.267 --> 29:49.184
[Seok-jin] Detective Kang!

605
29:49.268 --> 29:50.644
-[deliveryman] Get off! -Get off the bike.

606
29:50.728 --> 29:52.479
-[deliveryman] Come on! -Get off!

607
29:52.563 --> 29:54.607
-[strained grunt] -I'm sorry, sir.

608
29:54.690 --> 29:56.191
-Hey. -Are you hurt?

609
29:56.275 --> 29:57.526
Oh, hey there.

610
29:57.610 --> 29:58.819
You got the wrong person.

611
29:58.902 --> 30:00.279
The bad guy's getting away!

612
30:00.863 --> 30:02.698
-Whoa. -Hey, let's go.

613
30:04.575 --> 30:06.702
Why are you arresting me? I didn't do anything.

614
30:06.785 --> 30:08.329
I'm innocent!

615
30:08.412 --> 30:09.872
You are not innocent.

616
30:09.955 --> 30:12.166
And you made me run after you.

617
30:12.249 --> 30:13.709
You're a guilty person.

618
30:13.792 --> 30:14.752
-Let's go. -Come on.

619
30:14.835 --> 30:16.128
[Jae-hee] What's happening? I won't go!

620
30:16.211 --> 30:17.880
Go that way. I have to catch the guy.

621
30:17.963 --> 30:20.591
-[yells] I won't go! -[Wan-gu] Stop yelling.

622
30:21.425 --> 30:23.844
[gentle background music playing]

623
30:32.811 --> 30:34.897
The police won't be causing any more trouble.

624
30:35.522 --> 30:36.815
The chairman made a move.

625
30:36.899 --> 30:38.984
The shareholders' meeting is right around the corner,

626
30:39.068 --> 30:40.277
he can't have distractions.

627
30:43.197 --> 30:45.699
[sighs] If only Ms. Han hadn't caught onto it.

628
30:47.618 --> 30:49.495
All eyes will be on you for a while.

629
30:50.579 --> 30:51.789
This complicates things.

630
30:52.289 --> 30:55.042
Keep a low profile so we can minimize the risk.

631
30:57.920 --> 30:58.921
How thrilling.

632
30:59.463 --> 31:01.882
I guess everyone will get a look at me then.

633
31:14.770 --> 31:17.272
[upbeat intense music playing]

634
31:36.166 --> 31:39.795
TAEKANG, A $2.2 BILLION SAUDI PLANT CONTRACT

635
31:39.878 --> 31:41.547
Sleazebag rich kid.

636
31:41.630 --> 31:43.632
YOON MAKES BOLD MOVES IN SAUDI…

637
31:45.676 --> 31:48.137
TAEKANG YOON YI-JUN

638
31:48.220 --> 31:49.096
YOON YI-JUN

639
31:49.179 --> 31:51.140
YOON YI-JUN SIGNALS A NEW GENERATION OF LEADERSHIP IN TAEKANG?

640
31:51.223 --> 31:52.141
[Jae-hee] Wow.

641
31:52.224 --> 31:53.142
How much did he pay people

642
31:53.225 --> 31:55.644
to make sure not a single article about the incident got out?

643
31:57.980 --> 32:01.316
YOON YI-JUN'S SECRETARY

644
32:01.400 --> 32:02.776
BECOMING A SECRETARY

645
32:02.860 --> 32:04.987
TAEKANG GROUP, RECRUITING TF TEAM SECRETARY

646
32:06.613 --> 32:09.867
[low suspenseful music playing]

647
32:09.950 --> 32:10.868
Huh.

648
32:11.535 --> 32:14.455
[gate whirring]

649
32:40.522 --> 32:42.399
[Da-woon] Where exactly does it hurt?

650
32:42.983 --> 32:44.485
And when are you going to come into work?

651
32:45.861 --> 32:47.196
I'm so lonely there.

652
32:47.279 --> 32:49.448
The office feels empty now that you and Ms. Han aren't…

653
32:49.531 --> 32:51.492
[blabbers, grunts]

654
32:51.575 --> 32:52.826
-[cat meows] -[tuts]

655
32:53.952 --> 32:56.413
If you're lonely, why don't you cuddle Jerry?

656
32:56.914 --> 32:58.081
But before that,

657
32:58.165 --> 33:01.168
I'd say 400 lux of illumination should be adequate.

658
33:01.251 --> 33:02.211
What?

659
33:02.294 --> 33:06.548
I want to bask evenly in natural light at the perfect level of illumination.

660
33:06.632 --> 33:07.925
Hmm.

661
33:11.220 --> 33:12.054
Get out.

662
33:13.972 --> 33:14.848
[sharp sigh]

663
33:15.682 --> 33:18.185
[Da-woon mutters] What does he expect me to do, seriously?

664
33:21.271 --> 33:22.731
-Oh, you're here. -Yeah. Mm-hmm.

665
33:25.484 --> 33:26.485
[sighs]

666
33:26.568 --> 33:28.195
[soft snoring]

667
33:28.278 --> 33:31.406
Yep. As usual, our captain's the only one…

668
33:32.199 --> 33:33.700
sleeping on the job.

669
33:36.995 --> 33:38.789
-[slams] -Good morning.

670
33:38.872 --> 33:39.706
Oh.

671
33:39.790 --> 33:42.167
-Good morning, sir. -Ugh, you rotten punk.

672
33:43.752 --> 33:44.962
[hums]

673
33:47.339 --> 33:49.591
Hmm? Who's this for?

674
33:50.300 --> 33:51.218
[Jae-hee] Sir.

675
33:57.266 --> 33:58.100
YOON YI-JUN KILLED HER

676
33:59.309 --> 34:00.185
[mouse clicking]

677
34:01.311 --> 34:03.730
I thought I told you to stop being so clingy.

678
34:04.189 --> 34:06.358
Next time, you won't get off with just a warning.

679
34:08.193 --> 34:09.611
[Ms. Han] What are you gonna do?

680
34:12.823 --> 34:14.032
[Yi-jun] I don't know yet.

681
34:14.533 --> 34:15.993
If you were to keep this up…

682
34:16.535 --> 34:18.871
well, there's just no telling what I would do to you.

683
34:19.580 --> 34:20.414
[mouse clicks]

684
34:21.623 --> 34:23.709
Guess the rumors were true. They were going out.

685
34:26.044 --> 34:27.921
Uh, where are Wan-gu and Seok-jin right now?

686
34:28.005 --> 34:30.507
They just went to go visit the victim's family.

687
34:30.591 --> 34:32.050
-Get them back here. -Yes, sir.

688
34:37.055 --> 34:38.932
[Wan-gu] I'm sorry to trouble you.

689
34:39.016 --> 34:41.018
-[camera shutter clicks] -I just wanted to double-check.

690
34:41.643 --> 34:43.604
You're sure she wasn't acting any differently?

691
34:43.687 --> 34:46.523
And to your knowledge, she didn't receive any suspicious messages?

692
34:47.232 --> 34:48.984
Well, should you recall anything,

693
34:49.067 --> 34:50.777
even a minor detail,

694
34:50.861 --> 34:52.696
please feel free to reach out to me.

695
34:52.779 --> 34:55.866
Why was Ms. Han receiving your phone bill statements at her address?

696
34:57.826 --> 34:59.494
'Cause my sister used that phone.

697
35:00.662 --> 35:01.955
It was mine in name only.

698
35:02.039 --> 35:03.040
What?

699
35:03.874 --> 35:05.584
Ms. Han was using two separate cell phones?

700
35:06.960 --> 35:09.338
[low suspenseful music playing]

701
35:09.922 --> 35:12.341
So she had another phone of the same model.

702
35:12.424 --> 35:13.550
Yeah, that's right.

703
35:14.343 --> 35:15.510
Hey, how'd it go?

704
35:15.594 --> 35:18.680
Its last location was in the vicinity of Yoon Yi-jun's office.

705
35:19.723 --> 35:20.557
[sighs]

706
35:20.641 --> 35:24.686
Of her personal effects, this work phone was the only one which got to us.

707
35:25.312 --> 35:26.730
So where's that one gone?

708
35:26.813 --> 35:29.608
From what the family said, I'd guess that someone has hidden it.

709
35:30.567 --> 35:34.154
If we were to find that phone, it might count as direct evidence.

710
35:34.237 --> 35:35.155
[Jae-hee] That's right.

711
35:35.238 --> 35:38.367
It doesn't matter if Yoon Yi-jun and Han Eun-young were dating or not.

712
35:38.450 --> 35:40.786
If there's evidence on that phone, then we got him.

713
35:40.869 --> 35:42.079
TAEKANG SMARTPHONE K22 MEGA BLACK

714
35:42.162 --> 35:45.374
Yeah, and that's why we really need to find that phone.

715
35:45.457 --> 35:47.918
Let's just get a search warrant for Taekang and tear him--

716
35:48.001 --> 35:51.338
That way won't work. It won't help us find anything.

717
35:52.005 --> 35:54.675
Yeah, but with the higher-ups telling us to leave it alone

718
35:54.758 --> 35:56.593
and Taekang denying everything,

719
35:56.677 --> 35:58.136
what else can we do?

720
35:58.220 --> 35:59.596
We need to find that phone.

721
35:59.680 --> 36:01.974
[superior in angry voice] Where are those bastards?

722
36:02.057 --> 36:04.059
-Quick, hide everything! -[Jae-hee] Over here, sir!

723
36:04.142 --> 36:06.395
-[quirky music playing] -Whoa!

724
36:12.567 --> 36:13.610
What are you doing here?

725
36:13.694 --> 36:14.653
Meeting.

726
36:14.736 --> 36:15.737
Uh, not meeting.

727
36:15.821 --> 36:16.863
What kind of meeting?

728
36:17.948 --> 36:20.200
-Uh, well… Uh… -[superior] Huh?

729
36:20.951 --> 36:23.787
[grunts] We thought we should have a meeting.

730
36:24.287 --> 36:25.122
Uh… [clears throat]

731
36:25.205 --> 36:26.248
Um, about, uh…

732
36:26.873 --> 36:29.876
uh, if we should get delivery or go out to eat, sir.

733
36:30.293 --> 36:33.130
I'd say hamburgers are the perfect food, full of carbs, fat, protein, and fiber.

734
36:33.213 --> 36:35.007
Double cheeseburgers for all!

735
36:35.090 --> 36:36.383
Hello, is this the hamburger joint?

736
36:36.466 --> 36:37.551
[Captain Park] Hey, now…

737
36:38.218 --> 36:39.928
Would you like to join us, sir?

738
36:40.012 --> 36:41.555
What an absolute shit show.

739
36:41.638 --> 36:43.849
Wowee. I see you're all having fun.

740
36:43.932 --> 36:46.727
Where's the report for the Taekang Case? Huh?

741
36:46.810 --> 36:47.728
What?

742
36:48.228 --> 36:49.187
Does taking orders from a guy

743
36:49.271 --> 36:51.773
that's younger than you hurt your pride that much?

744
36:52.482 --> 36:53.358
Is that what it is?

745
36:55.402 --> 36:57.446
If I had that much pride to begin with,

746
36:57.529 --> 36:59.823
then I guess… I would outrank you…

747
37:00.907 --> 37:01.867
sir.

748
37:01.950 --> 37:03.618
Ugh, unbelievable.

749
37:05.078 --> 37:06.329
Get it to me by the end of the day.

750
37:08.081 --> 37:08.915
[groans]

751
37:10.250 --> 37:12.294
The victim's family's got their eyes on us,

752
37:13.045 --> 37:15.922
so if we were to sweep a chaebol case under the rug like this,

753
37:16.006 --> 37:17.215
they'd probably go to the press

754
37:17.299 --> 37:19.342
and accuse us of half-assing our investigation.

755
37:19.426 --> 37:20.677
They'll stone us for this.

756
37:20.761 --> 37:22.554
Even law enforcement needs to play it by the book

757
37:22.637 --> 37:24.097
if it wants some wiggle room.

758
37:24.181 --> 37:27.100
Hey, since we're about to get stoned, let's get stone pot rice.

759
37:27.184 --> 37:28.852
-Hello, stone pot rice joint. -Oh, cut it out.

760
37:31.146 --> 37:32.355
Whatever.

761
37:32.439 --> 37:34.775
-Fine, go fill up your schedule. -Hmm?

762
37:34.858 --> 37:36.234
If you come up empty,

763
37:36.985 --> 37:38.320
get ready for the consequences.

764
37:39.446 --> 37:41.281
-[raises voice] Got it? -[groans]

765
37:42.240 --> 37:44.576
Stone pot rice. You guys are driving me crazy.

766
37:44.659 --> 37:45.577
Forget it.

767
37:48.288 --> 37:50.373
-[door closes] -[sighs]

768
37:50.874 --> 37:53.043
Wow. That was insane.

769
37:53.543 --> 37:54.753
[Captain Park] Hey, we don't have much time.

770
37:55.670 --> 37:56.671
Got an angle?

771
37:58.381 --> 37:59.382
[tinks]

772
38:01.093 --> 38:02.594
I've got one, an angle.

773
38:04.221 --> 38:06.431
A job posting for a personal secretary.

774
38:06.890 --> 38:08.433
Take a look at this, Captain.

775
38:08.517 --> 38:10.060
"Taekang Group's TF team."

776
38:10.143 --> 38:12.604
That's the team Yoon Yi-jun is managing director of, right?

777
38:12.687 --> 38:15.482
"Duties include providing personal security.

778
38:15.565 --> 38:19.611
Preferred skills: martial arts expertise, security work," get it?

779
38:19.694 --> 38:20.821
If I could get that job,

780
38:20.904 --> 38:22.906
I could investigate from behind enemy lines.

781
38:22.989 --> 38:24.991
Get it? Get it? Get it? What do you think, huh?

782
38:25.075 --> 38:27.202
Get out of my face. You're making me sick.

783
38:27.285 --> 38:28.286
Stop it.

784
38:28.370 --> 38:30.205
-Can you do something about her? -Mm?

785
38:30.288 --> 38:31.915
Han Eun-young's missing phone.

786
38:32.541 --> 38:36.002
The missing cell phone that we have to locate, no matter what, right now.

787
38:36.670 --> 38:39.422
It's possible Yoon Yi-jun has it hidden somewhere close by.

788
38:39.506 --> 38:42.384
I mean, if Taekang's got everything covered in bulletproof glass,

789
38:42.467 --> 38:43.885
should we play by the book?

790
38:44.386 --> 38:45.804
You know that's not gonna fly.

791
38:45.887 --> 38:47.681
-You know that, right? -[Wan-gu] I do, I do.

792
38:48.348 --> 38:49.558
[Captain Park] I know that, okay?

793
38:50.058 --> 38:52.185
But we all blew our cover during the questioning.

794
38:52.853 --> 38:54.104
Why do you say "all"?

795
38:56.314 --> 38:57.399
One of us didn't.

796
39:07.200 --> 39:09.536
Yeah, but the posting said they're just hiring men.

797
39:09.619 --> 39:10.704
[Jae-hee] Hiring men.

798
39:10.787 --> 39:11.746
Men, huh?

799
39:12.664 --> 39:13.540
Yes.

800
39:14.374 --> 39:15.333
MAN

801
39:15.417 --> 39:17.002
[startled scream]

802
39:17.085 --> 39:19.004
[tense dramatic music playing]

803
39:19.087 --> 39:20.505
-[in firm voice] Men, huh? -Yeah.

804
39:21.715 --> 39:22.549
Come on.

805
39:22.632 --> 39:24.843
[in normal voice] I get mistaken all the time for being a guy, right?

806
39:24.926 --> 39:25.760
Although…

807
39:26.720 --> 39:28.346
I'm just acting naturally.

808
39:28.430 --> 39:29.306
-[sighs] -All right?

809
39:29.848 --> 39:31.641
[in firm voice] It's time! I'll man up!

810
39:31.725 --> 39:32.851
Just send me in!

811
39:32.934 --> 39:35.395
Ugh, do something about her. Cuff her or lock her up.

812
39:35.478 --> 39:38.106
I can't stand all this noise, seriously.

813
39:39.024 --> 39:39.858
Bravo.

814
39:40.817 --> 39:41.735
Hey, this could work!

815
39:42.235 --> 39:43.570
-Oh, no, not you too. -I mean…

816
39:43.653 --> 39:46.573
Kang's gotten into fights with men, and she's crushed them.

817
39:46.656 --> 39:48.700
[tires screeching]

818
39:48.783 --> 39:50.577
[tense dramatic music playing]

819
39:50.660 --> 39:51.912
Damn it. What's this?

820
39:52.662 --> 39:55.790
Hey, 3885. It's you, right?

821
39:56.750 --> 39:58.627
-[Jae-hee grunts] -[groans]

822
39:59.336 --> 40:00.337
[handcuffs click]

823
40:00.921 --> 40:01.963
[puffs]

824
40:02.047 --> 40:04.507
[dramatic music playing]

825
40:09.471 --> 40:10.972
I'll let you guys live.

826
40:12.432 --> 40:13.266
Hmm.

827
40:13.350 --> 40:16.061
Man, it's a good day to make an arrest.

828
40:20.190 --> 40:22.442
[tense Western-style music playing]

829
40:22.525 --> 40:23.944
Do you know who I am?

830
40:24.027 --> 40:25.195
[scoffs]

831
40:25.278 --> 40:26.655
-I'm Detective… -[groaning]

832
40:26.738 --> 40:30.659
[shouts] …Kang Jae-hee!

833
40:32.202 --> 40:34.412
[Wan-gu] I'm telling you, this is definitely going to work.

834
40:34.496 --> 40:35.914
-It'll work great! -[Captain Park] Oh, sure.

835
40:35.997 --> 40:37.999
It'd be good if she was by his side every day.

836
40:38.083 --> 40:40.085
You think Yoon Yi-jun would fall for that trick?

837
40:40.168 --> 40:41.169
Man.

838
40:41.253 --> 40:44.005
Sorry to interrupt, but your stew's ready.

839
40:46.466 --> 40:47.300
[owner chuckles]

840
40:47.384 --> 40:49.970
[owner] Um, I heard the strangest thing from our kitchen auntie,

841
40:50.053 --> 40:51.054
so I have to ask.

842
40:51.137 --> 40:52.931
Detective, are you a woman?

843
40:54.015 --> 40:55.517
Uh, yes. Yes, I am.

844
40:55.600 --> 40:57.811
-[Captain Park] Of course she is. -Heavens.

845
40:57.894 --> 41:00.272
She's been coming here for three years and I didn't know.

846
41:00.355 --> 41:02.065
-Hmm? -Gosh. [chuckles]

847
41:02.148 --> 41:04.567
She's so manly that I mistook her for a man. [laughs]

848
41:04.651 --> 41:06.194
-[Wan-gu] I know, right? -[laughter]

849
41:06.987 --> 41:09.239
-[Captain Park] Huh? -This is going to work.

850
41:11.491 --> 41:12.450
Well, Captain?

851
41:12.534 --> 41:15.120
Should be good enough to fool Yoon Yi-jun, right?

852
41:15.203 --> 41:18.540
A personal secretary doesn't just need to be good at martial arts.

853
41:18.623 --> 41:21.376
Are you capable of performing the basic duties?

854
41:21.459 --> 41:23.211
Well, as for that, I'll--

855
41:23.295 --> 41:25.463
Let's worry about that once she's passed the review.

856
41:26.464 --> 41:27.549
I'll provide backup.

857
41:29.384 --> 41:31.386
-You'll back me up? -You?

858
41:36.933 --> 41:37.767
Mm.

859
41:39.436 --> 41:40.687
If they reject you, that's it.

860
41:40.770 --> 41:41.855
Yep!

861
41:41.938 --> 41:43.023
All right then.

862
41:43.106 --> 41:44.607
I'll get to work on my résumé.

863
41:45.358 --> 41:46.192
Salute!

864
41:46.276 --> 41:47.402
Mm.

865
41:49.112 --> 41:50.613
Dude's so dead.

866
41:51.740 --> 41:52.574
[soft scoff]

867
41:55.660 --> 41:59.080
[uneasy music playing]

868
41:59.622 --> 42:00.749
[young Yi-jun] Mommy.

869
42:01.499 --> 42:02.792
Mommy.

870
42:02.876 --> 42:04.210
Mommy, wake up!

871
42:04.294 --> 42:05.253
-[gasps] -[music stops]

872
42:05.337 --> 42:07.589
[gasping]

873
42:08.965 --> 42:09.799
[clears throat]

874
42:12.510 --> 42:15.263
[heavy breathing]

875
42:17.557 --> 42:18.641
[deep exhale]

876
42:27.692 --> 42:29.069
What are you doing, buddy?

877
42:30.362 --> 42:31.696
Love.

878
42:31.780 --> 42:32.906
[tinkling]

879
42:32.989 --> 42:35.241
You're missing an E. What's up with the painting?

880
42:38.745 --> 42:40.705
It's more tilted than it was yesterday.

881
42:40.789 --> 42:43.124
Something had to physically shift it.

882
42:44.834 --> 42:47.045
[Si-hyun] What do you mean? Looks fine to me.

883
42:49.631 --> 42:50.757
Did you sleep enough?

884
42:51.257 --> 42:52.842
So what's this thing about hiring a new secretary?

885
42:52.926 --> 42:54.761
-[door opens] -[Da-woon] Mr. Yoon?

886
42:54.844 --> 42:56.012
[Si-hyun] Oh, yes, Mr. Jung.

887
42:57.514 --> 42:58.598
Welcome.

888
42:59.224 --> 43:00.266
This is so wrong, sir.

889
43:00.975 --> 43:02.894
What do you mean you don't care about academic background?

890
43:03.895 --> 43:04.813
Right.

891
43:05.355 --> 43:08.108
You do, in fact, excel in those departments, dear Mr. Jang.

892
43:08.191 --> 43:09.692
-Uh, it's Jung. -My name is Jung, sir.

893
43:11.027 --> 43:12.487
Folks who've done nothing but study

894
43:12.570 --> 43:14.030
tend to stop and think when danger strikes.

895
43:14.656 --> 43:15.657
So I'm going to skip them

896
43:15.740 --> 43:18.201
and choose from those with actual bodyguarding experience.

897
43:18.284 --> 43:19.953
[Da-woon] What about the desk work?

898
43:20.036 --> 43:23.164
What about me? I'm literally draining my next life's chi to meet my workload.

899
43:25.125 --> 43:25.959
So…

900
43:26.042 --> 43:26.918
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

901
43:27.627 --> 43:29.212
I can't take this anymore.

902
43:29.921 --> 43:31.881
Whoa, Mr. Jung, calm down.

903
43:31.965 --> 43:33.508
Take a moment to think it through.

904
43:33.591 --> 43:34.717
Don't try to talk me out of it.

905
43:34.801 --> 43:36.136
If you want to quit, you should do it.

906
43:36.636 --> 43:38.096
That is none of my concern.

907
43:38.179 --> 43:39.764
Great, then I'll just quit!

908
43:40.348 --> 43:43.184
Make sure to hand over your duties to your replacement, Mr. Choi.

909
43:43.268 --> 43:45.228
It's Jung, Mr. Yoon.

910
43:45.311 --> 43:47.939
Of course. Your name's Jung. Mr. Jung.

911
43:48.022 --> 43:49.941
I remembered it. I got it!

912
43:52.902 --> 43:54.446
[Da-woon] Way too overqualified.

913
43:54.529 --> 43:56.364
You're out. You're all out!

914
43:57.240 --> 43:58.199
Cut them all!

915
43:59.284 --> 44:00.410
[sighs]

916
44:07.125 --> 44:10.253
[Da-woon] Judo, hapkido, taekwondo. Level nine dan.

917
44:11.087 --> 44:12.255
He's good-looking enough,

918
44:12.338 --> 44:15.216
but has no secretarial experience whatsoever.

919
44:17.135 --> 44:18.803
But I think he needs to be humbled

920
44:18.887 --> 44:21.764
by having to work with an incompetent secretary.

921
44:21.848 --> 44:24.601
That's when he'll realize how good I was.

922
44:24.684 --> 44:25.768
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

923
44:25.852 --> 44:26.936
[phone chimes]

924
44:28.605 --> 44:30.690
I've got an interview. [laughs]

925
44:30.773 --> 44:31.774
Are you for real?

926
44:32.734 --> 44:34.569
-[laughs] -Come on, hand it over.

927
44:34.652 --> 44:36.070
Wow, good job!

928
44:36.154 --> 44:37.947
-[chuckles] -Hup hup, Bip Bop!

929
44:38.031 --> 44:38.907
[Jae-hee and Wan-gu] Ba-bang!

930
44:38.990 --> 44:39.991
TAEKANG GROUP: APPLICATION RESULTS

931
44:40.074 --> 44:42.785
[Wan-gu] See that? It worked. Just like I said it would.

932
44:42.869 --> 44:43.870
[scoffs]

933
44:45.538 --> 44:47.123
Why are you all standing around?

934
44:47.207 --> 44:49.083
-Ooh. -You need to go get ready.

935
44:49.167 --> 44:50.960
-Salute! -[Captain Park] Yep!

936
44:51.628 --> 44:53.087
[excited chuckle]

937
44:53.171 --> 44:55.006
This will help you. Take a look.

938
44:56.049 --> 44:57.217
[Seok-jin] Maintain eye contact.

939
44:57.300 --> 44:59.886
He may have reported the crime, he's still a suspect.

940
45:00.470 --> 45:01.346
After that…

941
45:01.429 --> 45:03.473
[upbeat music playing]

942
45:04.224 --> 45:05.391
Hold this for a second.

943
45:06.309 --> 45:07.769
I think you look best in this one.

944
45:11.064 --> 45:12.649
REPUBLIC OF KOREA ARMY KANG JAE-HEE

945
45:27.914 --> 45:29.123
[soft exhale]

946
45:31.668 --> 45:33.169
All right, Kang Jae-hee.

947
45:33.253 --> 45:35.088
Confidence… is the key.

948
45:35.838 --> 45:37.048
Let's go.

949
45:45.932 --> 45:46.849
[soft scoff]

950
45:50.103 --> 45:51.020
[exhales]

951
45:51.854 --> 45:53.273
[nervous exhale]

952
45:54.357 --> 45:58.820
"I will be there to support you to the best of my abilities

953
45:58.903 --> 46:00.738
so you can focus with me right by your side."

954
46:01.197 --> 46:03.032
[quirky upbeat music playing]

955
46:03.116 --> 46:04.075
Screw this company!

956
46:04.158 --> 46:06.369
Why, why, why, why?

957
46:08.079 --> 46:09.330
REJECTED

958
46:10.957 --> 46:12.542
Mom, this place is weird.

959
46:12.625 --> 46:13.835
-[applicant] I'm coming home. -It's weird?

960
46:14.294 --> 46:16.588
-It's weird? -[phone buzzes]

961
46:18.339 --> 46:19.507
[Seok-jin] How's it going?

962
46:20.008 --> 46:22.510
[Jae-hee] This place is… kinda weird…

963
46:22.594 --> 46:23.678
[Da-woon] Applicant Number Ten…

964
46:24.262 --> 46:25.513
Kang Jae-hee, we're ready.

965
46:25.597 --> 46:26.723
Oh, yep.

966
46:34.480 --> 46:35.732
[Da-woon] You may enter now.

967
46:40.945 --> 46:42.572
FORMER SPECIAL FORCES

968
46:42.655 --> 46:46.576
"This place is, dot, dot, dot, kinda weird, dot, dot, dot"?

969
46:47.285 --> 46:49.412
Man, that really is weird.

970
46:49.912 --> 46:52.749
What would a straight shooter like her use three dots for?

971
46:53.583 --> 46:56.002
Wait and see. She meets the qualifications,

972
46:56.586 --> 46:57.420
and she's prepared.

973
46:59.047 --> 47:00.548
[sighs]

974
47:05.219 --> 47:08.222
Applicant Ten, Kang Jae-hee. Hello.

975
47:10.099 --> 47:12.268
[tense music playing]

976
47:44.425 --> 47:45.760
-[blows air] -[music stops]

977
47:45.843 --> 47:47.512
[Jae-hee] What the heck? What a psycho.

978
47:48.721 --> 47:49.889
I guess I win.

979
47:50.556 --> 47:51.766
[Jae-hee] Why does he talk like that?

980
47:55.186 --> 47:56.604
[Yi-jun] You're a Special Forces veteran?

981
47:56.688 --> 47:58.606
-Yes, that is right. -[Yi-jun] Thought so.

982
47:58.690 --> 48:00.233
I could tell from your posture.

983
48:04.445 --> 48:05.530
Look at the photo,

984
48:05.613 --> 48:08.116
then point out three differences between it and here.

985
48:16.249 --> 48:17.166
Your interview starts now.

986
48:17.750 --> 48:18.710
Oh…

987
48:18.793 --> 48:20.878
[clock ticking]

988
48:44.318 --> 48:45.153
[buzzer buzzes]

989
48:45.236 --> 48:46.654
[Jae-hee] Ugh, I'm screwed.

990
48:47.280 --> 48:48.573
Thank you for your time.

991
48:49.073 --> 48:49.949
You can go.

992
48:50.825 --> 48:51.909
I found two differences.

993
48:51.993 --> 48:53.995
Oh, did you?

994
48:54.662 --> 48:56.706
Huh. All right. What did you find?

995
48:56.789 --> 48:59.000
The graph in the document on your desk is different.

996
48:59.792 --> 49:03.004
That, and the angle of the globe is tilted 15 degrees left.

997
49:13.723 --> 49:16.809
If you don't mind me asking, what was the last remaining discrepancy?

998
49:18.936 --> 49:19.854
There wasn't one.

999
49:22.190 --> 49:23.274
There were only two.

1000
49:25.568 --> 49:29.489
I just get a kick out of watching people look for something that doesn't exist.

1001
49:29.572 --> 49:30.573
I think it's funny.

1002
49:32.909 --> 49:34.911
You've got good observational skills.

1003
49:34.994 --> 49:38.039
To my knowledge, Special Forces get tasked with top-secret operations.

1004
49:38.831 --> 49:40.291
Have you ever killed someone?

1005
49:42.084 --> 49:42.919
What?

1006
49:44.587 --> 49:45.922
Have you killed anyone?

1007
49:46.631 --> 49:49.675
[low tense music playing]

1008
49:49.759 --> 49:53.262
I've been… obsessed… with it of late.

1009
49:55.515 --> 49:57.099
Are you saying that murder's…

1010
49:57.642 --> 49:58.851
on your mind?

1011
49:58.935 --> 49:59.852
[soft chuckle]

1012
50:00.812 --> 50:01.813
[clicks tongue]

1013
50:05.775 --> 50:06.984
[strained grunting]

1014
50:08.820 --> 50:11.322
[Ms. Han choking]

1015
50:18.996 --> 50:19.997
[heavy exhale]

1016
50:35.680 --> 50:37.139
You killed Eun-young, didn't you?

1017
50:40.142 --> 50:42.478
[ominous chuckling]

1018
50:48.860 --> 50:49.777
[music stops]

1019
50:53.573 --> 50:55.408
You've got guts, spacing out like that in here.

1020
50:55.491 --> 50:56.826
So what's your answer?

1021
51:00.329 --> 51:01.497
I guess you haven't.

1022
51:03.583 --> 51:05.084
I did witness a murder.

1023
51:07.503 --> 51:08.921
So, what was the situation?

1024
51:09.005 --> 51:11.424
Be honest. I'll give you bonus points.

1025
51:18.556 --> 51:20.892
We were rescuing a hostage, and the casualty…

1026
51:22.268 --> 51:23.269
was my senior.

1027
51:23.853 --> 51:24.979
-[senior] Kang Jae-hee! -[gunshots]

1028
51:25.938 --> 51:27.189
-Please let me live. -[gasps]

1029
51:30.359 --> 51:31.235
[squelches]

1030
51:31.319 --> 51:32.778
Sergeant Ko!

1031
51:33.362 --> 51:35.406
[screams] No!

1032
51:37.158 --> 51:38.534
[cries]

1033
51:39.994 --> 51:41.245
[Yi-jun] Ah…

1034
51:41.329 --> 51:44.790
So what determined his fate came down to a split-second decision,

1035
51:44.874 --> 51:46.542
and if you'd hesitated for a second less,

1036
51:46.626 --> 51:49.712
there's a chance he would still be alive with us today.

1037
51:52.131 --> 51:54.550
So, soldier, did you get him?

1038
51:54.634 --> 51:56.636
The prick who killed your senior?

1039
52:04.101 --> 52:05.561
It appears you didn't.

1040
52:05.645 --> 52:07.313
[tuts, sucks teeth]

1041
52:07.396 --> 52:11.192
Hmm, I bet he's living it up somewhere without a hint of remorse too.

1042
52:14.320 --> 52:16.989
Why don't we try something fun? Back up a bit.

1043
52:20.368 --> 52:21.369
Let's try this.

1044
52:21.786 --> 52:23.788
I want you to imagine what you would do

1045
52:24.205 --> 52:25.957
if you ever ran into that bastard again.

1046
52:29.460 --> 52:31.796
He's approaching you from five meters ahead.

1047
52:31.879 --> 52:34.382
Three meters, you have made eye contact.

1048
52:34.465 --> 52:37.635
Two meters, it's clear he remembers you and your senior.

1049
52:38.219 --> 52:39.553
One meter, what's this?

1050
52:39.637 --> 52:41.097
He's grinning at you.

1051
52:41.180 --> 52:43.599
And now, zero meters…

1052
52:43.683 --> 52:45.351
[tense music playing]

1053
52:56.737 --> 52:59.699
You made it out alive, I see. [echoing]

1054
52:59.782 --> 53:02.118
[tense music continues]

1055
53:02.201 --> 53:03.577
[gunshots]

1056
53:09.333 --> 53:10.167
7TH SPECIAL MISSION UNIT

1057
53:12.670 --> 53:14.005
[screams] No!

1058
53:16.215 --> 53:17.842
[Yi-jun yelps, grunts]

1059
53:18.592 --> 53:21.178
[groaning]

1060
53:21.929 --> 53:23.389
-[comical music playing] -[coughs]

1061
53:24.306 --> 53:25.349
[groans]

1062
53:25.433 --> 53:26.434
[gasps]

1063
53:27.018 --> 53:28.227
Oh, uh…

1064
53:29.061 --> 53:30.521
Oh, it hurts, doesn't it?

1065
53:30.604 --> 53:31.939
-Are you okay? -[groans]

1066
53:32.523 --> 53:34.025
You're gonna have trouble getting up.

1067
53:37.653 --> 53:38.988
[sighs]

1068
53:39.071 --> 53:40.114
[heavy exhale]

1069
53:40.656 --> 53:41.907
Rejected.

1070
53:43.492 --> 53:46.203
A personal secretary should never attack their boss, no matter what.

1071
53:46.787 --> 53:47.705
You're not qualified.

1072
53:48.831 --> 53:49.665
[sighs]

1073
53:49.749 --> 53:51.792
Go with Number Nine. I'm going home now.

1074
53:53.044 --> 53:54.086
[groans]

1075
53:54.545 --> 53:55.713
[Jae-hee] Dang it!

1076
53:55.796 --> 53:56.672
Stay back!

1077
54:01.093 --> 54:04.263
Oh, they warned you he might try something like this.

1078
54:04.346 --> 54:05.890
[breathes deeply]

1079
54:05.973 --> 54:08.726
Kang Jae-hee… you were so close to getting in.

1080
54:08.809 --> 54:10.061
You were almost there.

1081
54:13.647 --> 54:14.523
[sighs]

1082
54:16.901 --> 54:19.070
[breathes deeply]

1083
54:20.196 --> 54:21.405
Hide! It's Yi-jun!

1084
54:22.073 --> 54:24.366
-[woman 1 gasps] There he is! -[man] Yoon Yi-jun!

1085
54:24.450 --> 54:26.160
-[indistinct clamoring] -Bring my daughter back!

1086
54:26.243 --> 54:28.037
[Ms. Han's mom] Bring my daughter back to me!

1087
54:28.120 --> 54:29.497
[staff] Hey, hey, hey, keep away from him!

1088
54:29.580 --> 54:31.415
[woman 2] You won't get away with this, Yoon Yi-jun!

1089
54:31.499 --> 54:32.917
-[staff] Stay back! -[man] Yoon Yi-jun!

1090
54:33.000 --> 54:34.210
You damn murderer!

1091
54:34.293 --> 54:35.294
[tense music swells]

1092
54:36.087 --> 54:39.090
-[knife clatters] -[Ms. Han's brother groaning]

1093
54:39.173 --> 54:41.050
[panting] Let go!

1094
54:41.717 --> 54:42.885
Let go!

1095
54:42.968 --> 54:45.054
You were the only one there, I know you killed her!

1096
54:45.638 --> 54:48.182
[sobbing] You killed my sister!

1097
54:48.265 --> 54:49.517
[Ms. Han's brother] Let go!

1098
54:49.600 --> 54:50.768
That's not Kang, is it?

1099
54:51.185 --> 54:53.062
-[Ms. Han's brother wails] -[sighs] Shit.

1100
54:53.145 --> 54:56.357
Bring my sister back! Bring her back! [crying]

1101
54:56.440 --> 54:58.526
[Ms. Han's brother] I know you killed her.

1102
54:58.609 --> 54:59.443
Hey, are you okay?

1103
54:59.527 --> 55:00.611
[heavy exhale]

1104
55:01.821 --> 55:02.822
You.

1105
55:03.656 --> 55:05.116
You're that veteran from earlier.

1106
55:05.616 --> 55:06.826
Yes, that's right.

1107
55:06.909 --> 55:08.369
Why'd you intervene?

1108
55:08.452 --> 55:10.663
Those people there, do you know them?

1109
55:10.746 --> 55:11.789
I do not.

1110
55:11.872 --> 55:14.416
I just prioritized lending you my aid, that's all.

1111
55:15.793 --> 55:17.670
You're a pretty fast learner.

1112
55:18.462 --> 55:19.713
What to do?

1113
55:19.797 --> 55:21.340
You're the first one, you know.

1114
55:22.341 --> 55:24.927
The first to jump in harm's way to save me.

1115
55:30.516 --> 55:32.643
And the first to snap my back like a folder.

1116
55:32.726 --> 55:34.728
[Jae-hee] It's not too late to change your mind.

1117
55:34.812 --> 55:36.772
That's why I saved you.

1118
55:36.856 --> 55:38.482
What to do?

1119
55:40.067 --> 55:41.068
Hmm.

1120
55:42.278 --> 55:44.280
If you were a woman, I may have fallen for you.

1121
55:46.240 --> 55:48.576
[Jae-hee] Uh… I'm a man, sir.

1122
55:51.036 --> 55:52.288
Regardless of gender,

1123
55:52.371 --> 55:55.541
my personal secretary has to prioritize me above all else.

1124
55:55.624 --> 55:57.001
In order for that to work,

1125
55:57.084 --> 55:58.794
you are required to like me

1126
55:58.878 --> 56:00.462
completely and unconditionally.

1127
56:00.546 --> 56:01.755
Think you can do that?

1128
56:01.839 --> 56:03.007
I can, sir.

1129
56:03.090 --> 56:05.259
I'll prioritize you no matter the situation.

1130
56:05.342 --> 56:06.468
And?

1131
56:06.552 --> 56:09.013
No matter what, I'll try not to hate you.

1132
56:11.098 --> 56:12.641
And stay…

1133
56:12.725 --> 56:14.351
loyal to…

1134
56:14.435 --> 56:16.395
[comical music playing]

1135
56:16.478 --> 56:18.397
-[engine starts] -I will like you, sir!

1136
56:18.898 --> 56:19.940
Ugh, that came out wrong.

1137
56:22.067 --> 56:23.235
I like you, sir!

1138
56:24.445 --> 56:25.279
[Jae-hee] Oh…

1139
56:26.739 --> 56:27.740
[gasps]

1140
56:34.205 --> 56:37.124
Report to my residence. Monday at 9:00 a.m.

1141
56:44.590 --> 56:47.009
Man, I practically sold my soul just now.

1142
56:47.843 --> 56:50.095
I'm gonna get you no matter what, Yoon Yi-jun.

1143
56:51.305 --> 56:52.640
-[claps] -Whoa!

1144
56:52.723 --> 56:53.724
[shouts] Yeah!

1145
56:53.807 --> 56:56.060
[Captain Park laughing]

1146
56:56.143 --> 56:58.896
Kang Jae-hee, I never doubted you even for a second.

1147
56:58.979 --> 57:01.440
The captain never trusted you for even a second.

1148
57:01.523 --> 57:03.442
[laughing]

1149
57:04.485 --> 57:05.527
[coughing]

1150
57:07.446 --> 57:08.864
Brace yourselves, everyone.

1151
57:08.948 --> 57:10.491
We are now undercover

1152
57:10.574 --> 57:12.785
inside the largest company in Korea.

1153
57:12.868 --> 57:15.621
As you all know, evidence collected illegally is invalid,

1154
57:15.704 --> 57:17.039
so let's get everything we can.

1155
57:17.122 --> 57:18.999
-Mm. -[Seok-jin] This is only the beginning.

1156
57:19.083 --> 57:21.252
Let's catch the killer and give the victim some peace.

1157
57:21.335 --> 57:22.586
-[exhales] -The lost phone,

1158
57:22.670 --> 57:23.837
I'll find it no matter what.

1159
57:23.921 --> 57:25.923
-Leave it up to me! -Let's go!

1160
57:26.006 --> 57:27.049
Hold on.

1161
57:27.800 --> 57:29.468
Okay. As of right now,

1162
57:29.551 --> 57:31.095
you're forbidden from drinking alcohol.

1163
57:31.178 --> 57:33.430
[soft chuckle] I'll start tomorrow.

1164
57:33.514 --> 57:34.348
You start today.

1165
57:35.224 --> 57:37.768
You'll blow this operation to hell the moment you get drunk.

1166
57:37.851 --> 57:38.852
Is that clear?

1167
57:39.979 --> 57:41.105
Now then.

1168
57:41.188 --> 57:43.857
[Captain Park] Man, that place used to have the best pork belly.

1169
57:43.941 --> 57:45.401
-[Wan-gu] I'm so full. -[Seok-jin] Well done.

1170
57:47.695 --> 57:49.363
Without you, we wouldn't have had a chance.

1171
57:49.446 --> 57:51.490
[soft chuckle] I didn't do much.

1172
57:54.243 --> 57:55.828
Yoon Yi-jun won't be an easy mark.

1173
57:56.704 --> 58:00.207
From what the captain said, his interrogation was tough.

1174
58:01.417 --> 58:03.502
[soft music playing]

1175
58:03.585 --> 58:06.213
He can't keep his thoughts hidden while pushing your buttons.

1176
58:06.672 --> 58:09.174
I'll dig deep and see if he really did hide the phone somewhere.

1177
58:09.967 --> 58:12.720
Call me if you need to. I'll head right over.

1178
58:14.430 --> 58:16.140
Are you actually worried about me?

1179
58:16.807 --> 58:17.641
Huh?

1180
58:18.142 --> 58:19.476
You're worried, right?

1181
58:22.479 --> 58:26.400
7TH SPECIAL MISSION UNIT KANG JAE-HEE

1182
58:26.483 --> 58:27.568
7TH SPECIAL MISSION UNIT

1183
58:29.445 --> 58:30.988
KANG JAE-HEE

1184
58:33.699 --> 58:35.200
It's more torn up than I thought it was.

1185
58:36.201 --> 58:37.703
There's no helping it now.

1186
58:45.502 --> 58:49.089
KUNMANDU

1187
58:49.173 --> 58:51.133
[Jae-hee's dad] Why can't you make a meal like this all the time, huh?

1188
58:51.216 --> 58:52.968
[Jae-hee's mom] Well, 'cause it's way too much work, okay?

1189
58:53.052 --> 58:54.595
Wow, that smells delicious.

1190
58:54.678 --> 58:56.388
-[Jae-hee giggles] -[Jae-hee's mom chuckles]

1191
58:56.472 --> 58:58.182
-Come, have a seat. -Mm-hmm. Join us.

1192
58:58.891 --> 59:01.352
-[Jae-hee's mom] Mm, grab a seat. -Oh, wow.

1193
59:01.435 --> 59:02.436
[Jae-hee's mom] Here.

1194
59:03.103 --> 59:05.439
-Wow, you did it again, Mom. -[Jae-hee's mom chuckles]

1195
59:07.024 --> 59:08.359
Hey, what about the old one?

1196
59:08.442 --> 59:09.610
Oh, it's at the dry cleaners,

1197
59:09.693 --> 59:11.445
so I didn't have anything to wear tomorrow.

1198
59:11.528 --> 59:13.572
What's this about you not being able to visit?

1199
59:14.156 --> 59:15.574
It's related to a case.

1200
59:15.657 --> 59:17.910
So as usual, my lips are sealed.

1201
59:17.993 --> 59:18.994
[groans]

1202
59:19.495 --> 59:20.913
It's not dangerous, is it?

1203
59:20.996 --> 59:23.248
Oh, come on. What are you worried about?

1204
59:23.332 --> 59:26.168
Think of all the money our princess has had to pay in damages.

1205
59:26.251 --> 59:28.587
You should be worried for the guy she's up against.

1206
59:28.670 --> 59:29.588
Really, come on.

1207
59:31.548 --> 59:34.760
Yes, and if it weren't for Jae-hee, we would've been out on the streets

1208
59:34.843 --> 59:37.679
when you ran your loser chicken farm into the ground.

1209
59:37.763 --> 59:40.557
If you have a conscience, let her have the galbi, okay?

1210
59:42.226 --> 59:45.354
If you have a conscience, you should let her have the bossam too.

1211
59:45.437 --> 59:47.314
What's the problem?

1212
59:47.398 --> 59:49.108
Princess, do you mind if I eat some of this?

1213
59:49.191 --> 59:51.902
Sure. Here you go, Papa. Let me feed you some.

1214
59:51.985 --> 59:53.987
-Open up here. -Oh my.

1215
59:54.822 --> 59:57.324
-[scoffs] -You should be grateful to be a princess.

1216
59:57.991 --> 59:58.826
Why is that?

1217
59:58.909 --> 59:59.743
I wanna tell you,

1218
59:59.827 --> 01:00:01.703
this face was the neighborhood heartbreaker back in the day.

1219
01:00:01.787 --> 01:00:03.455
It's where you got your good looks.

1220
01:00:03.539 --> 01:00:04.665
You should be grateful to me.

1221
01:00:05.874 --> 01:00:06.917
She looks like me.

1222
01:00:07.000 --> 01:00:08.377
[chuckles] Oh, yeah, sure.

1223
01:00:08.460 --> 01:00:10.712
-Of you, Mom? -[both laughing]

1224
01:00:10.796 --> 01:00:14.133
Dad, just go with it. It's your only way out of it.

1225
01:00:14.216 --> 01:00:16.635
[all laughing]

1226
01:00:29.189 --> 01:00:30.315
I wanna know…

1227
01:00:31.525 --> 01:00:34.528
do you also believe that I'm the killer who murdered Ms. Han?

1228
01:00:45.664 --> 01:00:47.749
[low unsettling music playing]

1229
01:01:07.769 --> 01:01:09.688
[Jae-hee] I've arrived. Are we good?

1230
01:01:09.771 --> 01:01:11.440
[Seok-jin] Uh-huh. Visuals are clear.

1231
01:01:17.196 --> 01:01:18.447
[sharp exhale]

1232
01:01:20.240 --> 01:01:21.325
Then I'm going in.

1233
01:01:21.408 --> 01:01:23.076
[Seok-jin] Okay. Be careful.

1234
01:01:23.827 --> 01:01:25.579
[doorbell chimes]

1235
01:01:27.748 --> 01:01:30.083
[gate whirring]

1236
01:02:16.296 --> 01:02:18.382
Starting today, I'll be your personal secretary.

1237
01:02:18.465 --> 01:02:19.633
Kang Jae-hee reporting.

1238
01:02:25.764 --> 01:02:28.433
[sighs] I'm afraid this won't do, soldier.

1239
01:02:30.644 --> 01:02:31.812
It seems that…

1240
01:02:32.271 --> 01:02:34.106
I mean, I wasn't sure.

1241
01:02:34.189 --> 01:02:35.524
[Jae-hee] Oh, no way…

1242
01:02:37.359 --> 01:02:39.695
[tense music playing]

1243
01:02:45.993 --> 01:02:46.994
But…

1244
01:02:50.122 --> 01:02:52.624
[upbeat suspenseful music playing]

1245
01:03:01.675 --> 01:03:03.302
…you've been caught red-handed.

1246
01:03:04.052 --> 01:03:05.470
[Jae-hee] Is my cover blown?

1247
01:03:12.311 --> 01:03:14.313
[handcuffs rattling, click]

1248
01:03:16.315 --> 01:03:19.234
[closing theme music playing]

1249
01:03:38.503 --> 01:03:40.255
SPECIAL THANKS TO JUNG YOO-MIN AND PARK JUN-MUYN

1250
01:03:40.339 --> 01:03:42.299
-[Yi-jun] I'll keep a constant eye on you. -Jeez…

1251
01:03:42.382 --> 01:03:44.426
And you'll have to keep proving yourself to me.

1252
01:03:44.509 --> 01:03:47.012
[Jae-hee] Oh, he's even crazier than I thought he was.

1253
01:03:47.095 --> 01:03:48.472
[Captain Park] You might have to beat him up.

1254
01:03:48.555 --> 01:03:50.515
[Si-hyun] I heard the VIPs will be in the chairman's office.

1255
01:03:50.599 --> 01:03:51.516
Everyone, out.

1256
01:03:51.600 --> 01:03:53.560
[woman] I'm the chairman's executive secretary.

1257
01:03:53.644 --> 01:03:55.479
The Taekang Goddess is totally my type physically,

1258
01:03:55.562 --> 01:03:57.439
but her personality sucks.

1259
01:03:57.522 --> 01:03:59.107
She saw something before she died?

1260
01:03:59.191 --> 01:04:00.984
You got rid of everything Ms. Han saw, right?

1261
01:04:01.068 --> 01:04:02.319
[Captain Park] The missing phone is the key.

1262
01:04:02.402 --> 01:04:04.279
[Yi-jun] The room on the second floor is off-limits.

1263
01:04:04.363 --> 01:04:06.406
-[Jae-hee] That's the one. -Who are you?

1264
01:04:06.490 --> 01:04:07.824
[Yi-jun] Who sent you?
